Package: plantstressR
Title: Multivariate Phenotyping of Plant Stress Response Signatures
Version: 0.5.1
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Joao Everthon da Silva",
           family = "Ribeiro",
           email = "everthonribeiro10@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Quantifies the physiological signature of abiotic stress in plants
    from trait tables measured under control and stress treatments. Individual
    traits are converted into a signed, standardized Stress Response Index whose
    sign is oriented so that positive values always denote stress-induced
    impairment; trait indices are then combined into a weighted integrated
    stress index that ranks genotypes or treatments, displayed as heat map or
    radar signatures, and connected in regularized partial-correlation networks
    whose modules reveal traits that respond jointly to stress. The
    standardized-difference formulation of the trait index follows the
    stress-tolerance selection framework of Fischer and Maurer (1978)
    <doi:10.1071/AR9780897>, the network layer estimates shrinkage-regularized
    partial correlations within the partial-correlation network framework
    reviewed by Epskamp and Fried (2018) <doi:10.1037/met0000167>, and trait
    modules are detected with the multi-level modularity algorithm of Blondel
    and others (2008) <doi:10.1088/1742-5468/2008/10/P10008>. Randomized
    complete block designs are supported throughout, and an optional 'shiny'
    dashboard runs the whole workflow without writing code.
